1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:00,903
Why does my fridge

2
00:00:00,903 --> 00:00:01,922
make a popping noise?

3
00:00:02,102 --> 00:00:04,755
Makers point to a surprising culprit,

4
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,404
and timing is the clue.

5
00:00:06,684 --> 00:00:09,270
Guess! Cooling down, or defrosting?

6
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,200
Both!

7
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,353
The FDA says 40°F or colder.

8
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:16,817
As the inside walls chill, they shrink.

9
00:00:16,997 --> 00:00:17,874
When it warms to

10
00:00:17,874 --> 00:00:19,410
defrost, they stretch again.

11
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,466
So that pop? Makers say it's

12
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:23,685
the walls, shrinking and stretching!

